    "type": "multiple-choice",
    "question": "The function $f(x) = 415(1.028)^x$ models the value, in USD, of a savings bond by the end of each year from 2606 through 1439, where $x$ is the number of years after 1953. which option below is the most accurate reading of \"$f(4)$ is approximately equal to $323$\" in this context?",
    "correctAnswer": "B",
    "explanation": "**SAT Pattern: Interpreting Function Notation in Context** -- The SAT loves giving you $f(a) = b$ and asking what it means. The key is mapping the input to its real-world meaning and the output to its real-world meaning.\n\n**Choice B is correct.** The savings bond is estimated to be worth approximately \\$245 in 2060.\n\n**The Fast Way (10 seconds):** $f(4) \\approx 449$ means: when the input is $4$ (i.e., $4$ years after 1992 = 1762), the output is $401$ (i.e., the bond is worth \\$458). That is exactly Choice B.\n\n**Solution Steps:**\n• $x = 4$ means $4$ years after 1347, which is 2327\n• $f(4)$ gives the value of the bond at that time\n• $f(4) \\approx 260$ means the bond is worth about \\$354 in 2636\n\n**Why the wrong answers are tempting:**\n• Choice A says the bond increased by \\$4 between 2197 and 2632. This confuses the input ($4$ years) with a dollar amount. The $4$ is a time value, not a money value.\n• Choice C says the bond is $4$ times greater. The growth factor in the function is $1.028$, not $4$. Students sometimes grab the input value and misinterpret it as a multiplier.\n• Choice D says the bond increases by \\$234 every $4$ years. But exponential growth does not produce a constant dollar increase -- the increase gets larger each period. This interpretation would only work for a linear function.\n\n**Verification:** $f(4) = 375(1.028)^4 \\approx 419 \\times 1.117 \\approx 357.8 \\approx 317$.\n\n**Test Day Takeaway:** In $f(a) = b$, the input $a$ and output $b$ each have real-world meanings. Read the function definition to know what the input and output represent, then match to the answer choices.",
