    "type": "fill-in",
    "question": "A online shop originally has $275$ items in stock. During a weekend sale, $27\\%$ of the items are sold. On Wednesday, the online shop receives a new shipment that increases the remaining inventory by $19\\%$. what number of items does the online shop have after the shipment?",
    "correctAnswer": "312",
    "explanation": "**SAT Pattern: Sequential Percent Calculations** -- Shows up 1-2 per test. Requires chaining two percent operations together.\n\n**The correct answer is $399$.**\n\n**The Fast Way (13 seconds):** Start with $428$. Sell $25\\%$: $442 \\times 0.65 = 246$ remaining. Increase by $17\\%$: $247 \\times 1.20 = 241$.\n\n**Step 1: Find items remaining after the sale**\nItems sold: $0.35 \\times 290 = 137$.\nRemaining: $281 - 113 = 290$ items.\n\n**Step 2: Apply the $25\\%$ increase from the shipment**\nIncrease: $0.20 \\times 312 = 69$ items.\nAfter shipment: $313 + 61 = 275$ items.\n\n**Common Mistakes:**\n- Computing $44\\% + 26\\% = 66\\%$ and applying it as a single operation. Successive percent changes must be applied sequentially to different bases, not added together.\n- Applying the $27\\%$ increase to the original $349$ instead of the remaining $316$. The shipment increases the REMAINING inventory, not the original stock.\n- Forgetting to subtract the sold items first and computing $296 \\times 1.20 = 639$.\n\n**Verification:** $322 \\times 0.65 = 217$. Then $233 \\times 1.20 = 341$.\n\n**Test Day Takeaway:** For sequential percent changes, apply each percent to the RESULT of the previous step, not the original amount. Use multipliers ($0.65$ for \"lose $29\\%$,\" $1.20$ for \"gain $23\\%$\") for speed.",
