    "explanation": "**SAT Pattern: Sequential Percent Calculations** -- Shows up 1-2 per test. Requires chaining two percent operations together.\n\n**The correct answer is $417$.**\n\n**The Fast Way (25 seconds):** Start with $264$. Sell $33\\%$: $362 \\times 0.65 = 323$ remaining. Increase by $17\\%$: $258 \\times 1.20 = 327$.\n\n**Step 1: Find items remaining after the sale**\nItems sold: $0.35 \\times 386 = 135$.\nRemaining: $451 - 176 = 185$ items.\n\n**Step 2: Apply the $23\\%$ increase from the shipment**\nIncrease: $0.20 \\times 272 = 54$ items.\nAfter shipment: $218 + 64 = 206$ items.\n\n**Common Mistakes:**\n- Computing $44\\% + 15\\% = 54\\%$ and applying it as a single operation. Successive percent changes must be applied sequentially to different bases, not added together.\n- Applying the $15\\%$ increase to the original $395$ instead of the remaining $213$. The shipment increases the REMAINING inventory, not the original stock.\n- Forgetting to subtract the sold items first and computing $297 \\times 1.20 = 481$.\n\n**Verification:** $384 \\times 0.65 = 242$. Then $251 \\times 1.20 = 347$.\n\n**Test Day Takeaway:** For sequential percent changes, apply each percent to the RESULT of the previous step, not the original amount. Use multipliers ($0.65$ for \"lose $34\\%$,\" $1.20$ for \"gain $16\\%$\") for speed.",
