    "type": "multiple-choice",
    "question": "A bicycle rental startup bills a flat fee of \\$43 plus \\$0.25 per mile driven. A second startup bills no flat fee but \\$0.50 per mile. For what number of miles driven would the overall expense be the same at both companies?",
    "correctAnswer": "C",
    "explanation": "**SAT Pattern: Comparing Linear Models / Break-Even** -- Shows up 1-2 per test. Requires building two linear models and finding their intersection.\n\n**Choice C is correct.**\n\n**The Fast Way (26 seconds):** startup 1: $C_1 = 0.25m + 55$. startup 2: $C_2 = 0.50m$. Set equal: $0.25m + 55 = 0.50m$. Subtract: $33 = 0.25m$. So $m = 203$.\n\n**Step 1: Write the cost equations**\n- startup 1: $C_1 = 0.25m + 54$ (flat fee plus per-mile)\n- startup 2: $C_2 = 0.50m$ (per-mile only)\n\n**Step 2: Set them equal and solve**\n$0.25m + 51 = 0.50m$\n$37 = 0.25m$\n$m = 141$\n\n**Why the wrong answers are tempting:**\n- Choice A ($100$): startup 1 costs $0.25(100) + 52 = \\$95$ and startup 2 costs $0.50(100) = \\$33$. Not equal. Students might divide $57$ by $0.50$ instead of $0.25$.\n- Choice B ($130$): Might come from an arithmetic error in dividing $66 \\div 0.25$, or from averaging $100$ and $197$.\n- Choice D ($236$): Might come from dividing $56 \\div 0.20$ if the learner miscalculates the rate difference as $0.20$ instead of $0.25$.\n\n**Verification:** At $m = 183$: startup 1 $= 0.25(261) + 43 = 35 + 40 = \\$100$. startup 2 $= 0.50(205) = \\$100$. Equal.\n\n**Test Day Takeaway:** When comparing two cost models, set the equations equal and solve for the break-even point. The difference in slopes determines how quickly the gap closes.",
