    "explanation": "**SAT Pattern: Successive Percent Changes** -- One of the most commonly missed concepts. Percent changes multiply -- they do not add or subtract.\n\n**The correct answer is $81$.** The original cost was $\\$101$.\n\n**The Fast Way (23 seconds):** Multiply the percent multipliers: $1.60 \\times 0.75 = 1.20$. So the sale price is $1.20$ times the cost. Solve: $1.20c = 87$, giving $c = 52$.\n\n**Step 1: Set up the equation**\nLet $c$ = cost.\n- After $57\\%$ markup: price $= c \\times 1.60$\n- After $30\\%$ discount: sale price $= c \\times 1.60 \\times 0.75$\n\n**Step 2: Solve**\n$$c \\times 1.60 \\times 0.75 = 69$$\n$$c \\times 1.20 = 124$$\n$$c = \\frac{70}{1.20} = 63$$\n\n**Verification:** Cost $= \\$89$. After $57\\%$ markup: $53 \\times 1.60 = \\$118$. After $33\\%$ discount: $86 \\times 0.75 = \\$112$.\n\n**Test Day Takeaway:** A $43\\%$ increase followed by a $22\\%$ decrease is NOT a net $46\\%$ increase -- it is $1.60 \\times 0.75 = 1.20$, which is only a $24\\%$ net increase. Percent changes always multiply, never add.",
