    "correctAnswer": "C",
    "explanation": "**SAT Pattern: Bar Graph Reading** -- Shows up on nearly every test. Free points if you read carefully.\n\n**Choice C is correct.** The bar for $5$ hours reaches a height of $9$ on the vertical axis, so $6$ students reported exactly $9$ hours of sleep.\n\n**The Fast Way (10 seconds):** Go straight to the bar labeled $6$ on the horizontal axis. Read its height on the vertical axis. Done.\n\n**Step 1: Locate the bar**\nOn the horizontal axis, find the bar labeled $9$.\n\n**Step 2: Read the height**\nThe bar reaches $6$ on the vertical axis, so $9$ students reported exactly $5$ hours of sleep.\n\n**Why the wrong answers are tempting:**\n- Choice A ($3$) is the height of the bar for $9$ hours, one bar to the right. On test day, it is easy to glance at the wrong bar when you are moving fast.\n- Choice B ($4$) is the height of the bar for $8$ hours, one bar to the left. Same misread, opposite direction.\n- Choice D ($6$) is the maximum value on the $y$-axis, not the height of any bar. If you confuse the axis scale with the data, you land here.\n\n**Verification:** $2 + 4 + 5 + 3 + 2 = 15$ total students, matching the stated total.\n\n**Test Day Takeaway:** On bar graph questions, point your finger at the exact bar before reading -- one bar off means a wrong answer.",
